s-shown"><p class=3D"eq__verdict no">=E2=9C=97 Incorrect</p><div><!-- DOMAI=
N: Design Infrastructure Solutions -->
<p><b>Correct answer: Availability Set with Update Domain</b></p>
<p>Availability Sets are a data center configuration that ensures that at l=
east one virtual machine is available during planned or unplanned maintenan=
ce. An update domain is a group of VMs that are rebooted together during pl=
anned maintenance. By placing VMs in different update domains, Azure ensure=
s that not all VMs are rebooted at the same time. This addresses requiremen=
t 2, which specifies that the application should continue functioning even =
if the underlying hardware is rebooted. Using Availability Sets with Update=
 Domains ensures high availability within a single data center.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>A. Availability Zone</b> - Availability Zones are physically separate=
 locations within an Azure region. While they provide high availability, th=
ey protect against data center failures, not just hardware reboots within a=
 data center. Requirement 2 specifically addresses hardware reboots, making=
 Availability Sets a more suitable choice.</p>
<p><b>C. Availability Set with Fault Domain</b> - Fault domains provide pro=
tection from hardware failures within a data center, such as a power outage=
 or network switch failure. While related to availability, fault domains do=
 not directly address the scenario of planned maintenance reboots, which is=
 the focus of requirement 2. Update domains are specifically designed for t=
his purpose.</p>
<p><b>D. Virtual Machine Scale Set (VMSS)</b> - Virtual Machine Scale Sets =
allow you to create and manage a group of identical, load balanced VMs. Whi=
le VMSS can improve availability and scalability, they do not, on their own=
, guarantee that VMs will be spread across update domains to handle planned=
 maintenance reboots. They are often used in conjunction with Availability =
Zones or Availability Sets for high availability, but Availability Sets wit=
h Update Domains are the more direct solution for requirement 2.</p>
