=3D"eq__num">Question 2 of 100</div><div class=3D"eq__q"><p>Fabrikam is a c=
loud-only organization with 500 users all working remotely with 15 global a=
dministrators assigned to the tenant. They have 3 subscriptions which are m=
anaged by three different departments:<br>
=C2=B7 App1_Production which is managed by the development team<br>
=C2=B7 App2_Test which is managed by the administrator team<br>
=C2=B7 App3_B2B which is managed by a 3rd party</p>
<p>Fabrikam needs to assign role-based access control to these subscription=
s based on the following requirements:<br>
Requirement 1: App2_Test users should only be able to fully manage the solu=
tion including the permission to add additional users to the subscription w=
ith the permissions required<br>
Requirement 2: App3_B2B users should only be able to view resources in the =
subscription<br>
Requirement 3: App1_Production users should be able to fully manage the sol=
ution but should not be able to add additional users to the subscription<br=
>
Requirement 4: Decrease the amount of statically assigned Global Administra=
tors by means of access control management<br>
Requirement 5: Ensure users assigned RBAC permission to resources are revie=
wed on a regular basis to minimize stale role assignments<br>
Requirement 6: Decrease the amount of statically assigned RBAC users by mea=
ns of access control management<br>
Requirement 7: Allow only a specific 3rd party user to start and reboot vir=
tual machines, but not shutdown VMs.</p>
<p>Which of the following RBAC roles should you assign for requirement 1?</=
p></div><div><div class=3D"eq__opt is-locked"><span class=3D"eq__mark">A</s=
pan><span>Contributor role</span></div><div class=3D"eq__opt is-locked is-c=
orrect"><span class=3D"eq__mark">=E2=9C=93</span><span>Owner role</span></d=
iv><div class=3D"eq__opt is-selected is-locked is-wrong"><span class=3D"eq_=
_mark">=E2=9C=97</span><span>Global administrator role</span></div><div cla=
ss=3D"eq__opt is-locked"><span class=3D"eq__mark">D</span><span>Reader role=
</span></div></div><button class=3D"eq__btn eq__btn--sm eq__check" fdproces=
sedid=3D"srpw5" style=3D"display: none;">Check Answer</button><div class=3D=
"eq__expl is-shown"><p class=3D"eq__verdict no">=E2=9C=97 Incorrect</p><div=
><!-- DOMAIN: Design Identity, Governance, and Monitoring Solutions (25-30%=
) -->
<p><b>Correct answer: Owner role</b></p>
<p>The Owner role grants full access to manage all resources, including the=
 ability to delegate access to others. Requirement 1 states that App2_Test =
users should be able to fully manage the solution and add additional users =
with the required permissions. The Owner role is the only built-in role tha=
t satisfies this requirement. It encompasses all actions, including assigni=
ng roles to other users, which is essential for managing permissions within=
 the subscription.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>A. Global administrator role</b> - The Global Administrator role is a=
n Azure Active Directory role, not an Azure RBAC role applicable at the sub=
scription level. While Global Administrators have broad permissions across =
the Azure AD tenant, they do not automatically have Owner permissions on Az=
ure subscriptions. Assigning the Global Administrator role would not direct=
ly address the requirement of managing resources and permissions within the=
 App2_Test subscription. Furthermore, using Azure AD roles for subscription=
 management is not a best practice; RBAC should be used instead.</p>
<p><b>C. Contributor role</b> - The Contributor role allows users to create=
 and manage Azure resources, but it does not grant the ability to assign ro=
les to other users. Since Requirement 1 specifically states that users shou=
ld be able to add additional users to the subscription with the required pe=
rmissions, the Contributor role is insufficient.</p>
<p><b>D. Reader role</b> - The Reader role grants read-only access to Azure=
 resources. Users assigned the Reader role can view resources but cannot ma=
ke any changes or assign roles to others. This role clearly does not meet t=
he requirement of fully managing the solution and adding additional users.<=
/p>
