<p><b>Correct answer: Azure Data Lake Storage</b></p>
<p>Azure Data Lake Storage is designed for storing massive amounts of data =
in various formats (structured, semi-structured, and unstructured). It is a=
 scalable and cost-effective solution for data lakes, making it suitable fo=
r storing large volumes of data from diverse sources before further process=
ing or analysis. The requirement for Service2 is a "sustainable data store =
for taking large amounts of data," which aligns perfectly with the capabili=
ties of Azure Data Lake Storage.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>A. Azure Databricks</b> - Azure Databricks is an Apache Spark-based a=
nalytics service used for data processing and machine learning. While it ca=
n work with large datasets, it's not primarily a data storage solution. It'=
s more focused on data transformation and analysis.</p>
<p><b>B. Azure Data Factory</b> - Azure Data Factory is a data integration =
service that orchestrates and automates the movement and transformation of =
data. It's used for building ETL (Extract, Transform, Load) pipelines, but =
it's not a data storage solution itself. It moves data between different st=
orage systems.</p>
<p><b>C. Azure Analysis Services</b> - Azure Analysis Services is an online=
