<p><b>Correct answer: Azure AD Pass-through Authentication</b></p>
<p>Azure AD Pass-through Authentication (PTA) allows users to sign in to on=
-premises applications and services using the same passwords they use to si=
gn in to their on-premises Active Directory. Importantly, passwords are not=
 stored in Azure AD, satisfying the compliance requirement. PTA works by us=
ing lightweight agents installed on on-premises servers. When a user attemp=
ts to sign in, the agent validates the username and password against the on=
-premises Active Directory. Azure AD Conditional Access, including multi-fa=
ctor authentication (MFA), can be enforced when users access business-criti=
cal applications, fulfilling the security administrator's requirement.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
