 the requirement of not storing passwords in any format in the cloud enviro=
nment.</p>
<p><b>B. Active Directory Federation Services (AD FS)</b> - AD FS is a vali=
d option for federated identity, allowing on-premises AD to authenticate us=
ers. However, it requires more complex infrastructure and configuration com=
pared to Pass-through Authentication. While it doesn't directly store passw=
ords in Azure AD, it relies on the on-premises AD FS infrastructure for aut=
hentication. Pass-through Authentication is a simpler solution that also me=
ets the requirements.</p>
