<p><b>Correct answer: Self-service password reset</b></p>
<p>Self-service password reset (SSPR) allows users to reset their passwords=
 without administrator intervention. This significantly reduces the operati=
onal overhead associated with password management, as administrators no lon=
ger need to handle routine password reset requests. Azure AD Premium P1 (or=
 higher) is required for SSPR.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Correct answer: Password writeback</b></p>
<p>Password writeback allows password changes made in Azure AD (e.g., throu=
gh SSPR) to be written back to the on-premises Active Directory. This ensur=
es that users have a consistent password across both environments. Without =
password writeback, users would need to maintain separate passwords, increa=
sing administrative overhead and user frustration. Password writeback requi=
res Azure AD Connect and appropriate permissions.</p>
