s have appropriate access rights, not on simplifying password management.</=
p>
<p><b>D. Azure AD Privileged Identity Management policies</b> - Azure AD Pr=
ivileged Identity Management (PIM) is used to manage, control, and monitor =
access to important resources in the organization. While PIM is crucial for=
 securing privileged accounts, it does not directly reduce the operational =
overhead of managing regular user credentials. PIM focuses on just-in-time =
access and minimizing the attack surface for highly privileged roles, not o=
n streamlining password management for all users.</p>
