<p><b>Correct answer: Create a custom RBAC role</b></p>
<p>Creating a custom RBAC role is the correct solution because it allows fo=
r very granular control over permissions. In this scenario, the requirement=
 is to allow a specific 3rd party user to start and reboot virtual machines=
, but not shut them down. Predefined roles in Azure might not offer this sp=
