<p><b>C. Azure Active Directory Domain Services (AADDS)</b> - Azure Active =
Directory Domain Services provides managed domain services such as domain j=
oin, group policy, LDAP, and Kerberos/NTLM authentication. It is used to su=
pport legacy applications that require domain services. It does not provide=
 a mechanism for granting specific Azure resource permissions like starting=
 or rebooting VMs. It is not relevant to requirement 7.</p>
<p><b>D. RBAC at the Subscription level</b> - While RBAC is the foundation =
for access control in Azure, assigning a built-in role at the subscription =
level would likely grant more permissions than necessary. There is no built=
-in role that allows starting and rebooting VMs but prevents shutting them =
down. Using a built-in role at the subscription level would violate the pri=
nciple of least privilege and not meet the specific requirements of require=
ment 7.</p>
