<p><b>Correct answer: Azure Policy</b></p>
<p>Azure Policy is the correct choice because it allows you to enforce orga=
nizational standards and assess compliance at-scale. Specifically, Azure Po=
licy can be used to restrict the regions where virtual machines can be crea=
ted and to limit the sizes (SKUs) of virtual machines that can be deployed.=
 You can define policies that deny the creation of VMs in unauthorized regi=
ons or with unauthorized sizes. This ensures that developers adhere to the =
specified constraints when provisioning resources. Azure Policy definitions=
 are evaluated when resources are created or updated, providing real-time e=
nforcement of the defined rules.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>A. Azure Resource Manager Templates</b> - Azure Resource Manager (ARM=
) Templates define the infrastructure as code. While you can use ARM templa=
tes to specify the region and size of virtual machines, they do not inheren=
tly enforce these restrictions. Developers could still modify the template =
or deploy resources outside of the template, bypassing the intended constra=
ints. ARM templates are a deployment mechanism, not an enforcement mechanis=
m.</p>
<p><b>C. conditional access policies</b> - Conditional Access policies are =
used to control access to cloud applications based on certain conditions, s=
uch as user location, device, and application sensitivity. They are primari=
ly focused on identity and access management, not on restricting the deploy=
ment of Azure resources based on region or size.</p>
<p><b>D. role-based access control (RBAC)</b> - Role-based access control (=
RBAC) is used to manage access to Azure resources by assigning roles to use=
rs, groups, and service principals. While RBAC can control who has permissi=
on to create virtual machines, it does not provide a mechanism to restrict =
the regions or sizes of the virtual machines that can be created. RBAC focu=
ses on authorization (who can do what), not on constraints (what can be don=
e).</p>
