<p><b>Correct answer: Azure SQL Database Managed Instance</b></p>
<p>Azure SQL Database Managed Instance is the correct choice because it mee=
ts all the specified requirements. It provides automatic patching and versi=
on updates, automatic backups, high availability, a native VNET with privat=
e IP addressing, encryption of data in transit, and a single-tenant environ=
ment with dedicated underlying infrastructure. Managed Instance offers near=
 100% compatibility with on-premises SQL Server, simplifying migration. It =
handles the underlying infrastructure, allowing you to focus on database ad=
ministration and development.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>A. SQL Server in a Docker container running on Azure Container Instan=
ces (ACI)</b> - While ACI can run SQL Server in a Docker container, it does=
 not inherently provide automatic patching, version updates, or automatic b=
ackups. High availability would require additional configuration and manage=
ment. ACI is more suited for stateless applications and doesn't offer the s=
ame level of management features as Managed Instance for SQL Server.</p>
<p><b>B. SQL Server in Docker containers running on Azure Kubernetes Servic=
e (AKS)</b> - AKS provides orchestration for Docker containers, including S=
QL Server. However, like ACI, it doesn't inherently provide automatic patch=
ing, version updates, or automatic backups for SQL Server. While high avail=
ability can be configured, it requires more manual setup and management com=
pared to Managed Instance. AKS is a good option for containerized applicati=
ons but adds complexity for SQL Server management.</p>
<p><b>C. SQL Server Infrastructure-as-a-Service (IaaS) virtual machine (VM)=
</b> - While SQL Server on an IaaS VM provides a single-tenant environment =
and allows for VNET integration, it requires manual management of patching,=
 version updates, backups, and high availability. This option places the op=
erational burden on the user, which contradicts the requirement for automat=
ic services.</p>
<p><b>E. Azure SQL Database with elastic pools</b> - Azure SQL Database wit=
h elastic pools is a Platform-as-a-Service (PaaS) offering, but it is a mul=
ti-tenant environment, which violates the requirement for a single-tenant e=
nvironment with dedicated infrastructure. While it provides automatic patch=
ing, backups, and high availability, the shared infrastructure makes it uns=
uitable for this scenario.</p>
