<p><b>Correct answer: Event Grid</b></p>
<p>Event Grid is the correct choice because it's designed for event-based a=
rchitectures. It allows you to subscribe to specific events happening withi=
n Azure resources, such as resource creation or deletion in a resource grou=
p. You can then configure a handler, such as an email notification, to be t=
riggered when those events occur. Event Grid offers near real-time event de=
livery and is highly scalable, making it suitable for monitoring and reacti=
ng to changes in your Azure environment. You can create an Event Grid subsc=
ription scoped to the "Production" resource group, filtering for "Microsoft=
.Resources.ResourceWriteSuccess" and "Microsoft.Resources.ResourceDeleteSuc=
cess" events, and configure an email action to notify you.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>A. Event Hub</b> - Event Hubs is a data streaming platform and event =
