lications and devices. While it deals with events, it's not designed for re=
acting to Azure resource changes and triggering actions like email notifica=
tions. It requires a consumer application to process the events, making it =
less suitable for simple event-driven automation.</p>
<p><b>C. Resource Lock</b> - Resource Locks are used to prevent accidental =
deletion or modification of Azure resources. They do not provide eventing o=
r notification capabilities. They are a governance tool, not a monitoring o=
r automation tool.</p>
<p><b>D. Service Bus</b> - Service Bus is a messaging service that facilita=
tes communication between applications and services. While it can handle ev=
ents, it's more suited for complex messaging scenarios and decoupling appli=
cations. It's not the ideal choice for simply monitoring Azure resource eve=
nts and triggering email notifications, as Event Grid is specifically desig=
ned for this purpose with its built-in integration with Azure services and =
event filtering capabilities.</p>
