<p><b>Correct answer: ExpressRoute</b></p>
<p>ExpressRoute provides a dedicated, private network connection between yo=
ur on-premises infrastructure and Azure datacenters. This offers more relia=
ble and consistent performance, higher bandwidth, and lower latency compare=
d to VPN connections. Since the scenario emphasizes the need for reliable a=
nd consistent performance for business-critical applications, ExpressRoute =
is the most suitable solution. ExpressRoute connections bypass the public i=
nternet, which reduces the risk of unpredictable network performance and se=
curity vulnerabilities.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>B. Site-to-Site VPN</b> - A Site-to-Site VPN creates an encrypted con=
nection over the public internet between your on-premises network and an Az=
ure virtual network. While it provides secure connectivity, it relies on th=
e public internet, which can be subject to fluctuations in performance and =
latency. This makes it less suitable for business-critical applications req=
uiring consistent and reliable performance.</p>
<p><b>C. Point-to-Site VPN</b> - A Point-to-Site VPN allows individual clie=
nts (e.g., laptops) to connect securely to an Azure virtual network over th=
e internet. This is primarily designed for individual users needing remote =
access and is not appropriate for establishing a consistent, high-performan=
ce connection between an on-premises datacenter and Azure for application i=
ntegration.</p>
<p><b>D. All of these</b> - While all options provide connectivity to Azure=
, only ExpressRoute offers the dedicated, private connection necessary for =
reliable and consistent performance required by business-critical applicati=
ons as described in the scenario. Site-to-Site and Point-to-Site VPNs are n=
ot designed for this purpose.</p>
