<p><b>Correct answer: Az Copy tool</b></p>
<p>AzCopy is a command-line utility designed for copying data to and from A=
zure Storage. It's optimized for high-performance data transfer and support=
s resuming interrupted transfers. After the initial 10TB transfer (potentia=
lly using Azure Data Box or Azure Import/Export service), AzCopy can be use=
d for periodic transfers of smaller amounts of data (MBs). AzCopy can be sc=
ripted and automated for recurring transfers, making it suitable for ongoin=
g data synchronization or backups.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Correct answer: Azure Data Factory</b></p>
<p>Azure Data Factory (ADF) is a fully managed, serverless data integration=
 service. It allows you to create, schedule, and orchestrate data pipelines=
. After the initial large data transfer, ADF can be used to create pipeline=
s that periodically copy MBs of data to the Azure Storage account. ADF supp=
orts various connectors, including Azure Blob Storage, and provides feature=
s for data transformation and monitoring. It's a robust solution for managi=
ng recurring data transfer tasks.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>C. Azure EventHubs</b> - Azure Event Hubs is a real-time event ingest=
