<p><b>Correct answer: Integrated Authentication</b></p>
<p>Integrated Authentication, in the context of Azure Batch, refers to usin=
g the logged-in user's Azure Active Directory (Azure AD) credentials to aut=
henticate with the Batch account. This is typically achieved through the Az=
ure CLI or PowerShell, where the user has already authenticated to Azure. T=
he Batch service then leverages this existing Azure AD token to authorize a=
ctions. This simplifies authentication as it avoids the need for separate c=
redentials.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Correct answer: Service Principal</b></p>
<p>A Service Principal is an Azure AD identity created for use with applica=
tions, services, and automation tools. It allows you to grant specific perm=
issions to the Batch account without requiring a user to be logged in. This=
 is especially useful for automated tasks or background processes that need=
 to interact with the Batch service. You create a service principal in Azur=
e AD, assign it the necessary roles (e.g., Batch Account Contributor), and =
then use its credentials (client ID and client secret) to authenticate with=
 the Batch account.</p>
<br><br>
<p><b>Incorrect:</b></p>
<p><b>A. Basic Authentication</b> - Basic Authentication typically refers t=
o using a username and password directly for authentication. While Azure se=
rvices might have supported basic authentication in the past, it is general=
ly discouraged and often disabled for security reasons. Azure Batch primari=
ly uses Azure AD authentication mechanisms like Integrated Authentication a=
nd Service Principals for enhanced security and manageability.</p>
<p><b>B. Role Based Access</b> - Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) is an aut=
horization mechanism that defines what actions a user, group, or service pr=
incipal can perform on Azure resources. While RBAC is crucial for managing =
permissions and access to the Batch account, it is not an authentication te=
chnique itself. Authentication verifies the identity of the user or service=
 principal, while RBAC determines what they are allowed to do after authent=
ication.</p>
