e entire VM, not just the SQL Server databases. While it can perform differ=
ential backups, it's not optimized for SQL Server and doesn't provide appli=
cation-consistent backups for SQL Server, potentially leading to data incon=
sistencies. The question specifies backing up SQL server data, not the enti=
re VM.</p>
<p><b>C. SQL Server in Azure VM -&gt;Log backup</b> - This option is incorr=
ect because log backups only capture the transaction logs of the SQL Server=
 database. While transaction log backups are essential for point-in-time re=
covery, they cannot be used alone to restore a database. They require a ful=
l backup as a base. The question asks for a policy that backs up data that =
has changed since the full backup, which is the purpose of a differential b=
ackup, not a log backup.</p>
<p><b>D. Azure Virtual Machine policy - &gt; Full backup</b> - This option =
is incorrect because while it would back up the entire VM including the SQL=
 Server databases, it doesn't meet the requirement of backing up only the d=
ata that has changed since the last full backup. Full backups capture all d=
ata every time, leading to larger backup sizes and longer backup times comp=
ared to differential backups.</p>
