 the entire tenant, including Azure subscriptions, assigning this role to m=
eet requirement 3 would violate requirement 4 (decrease the number of Globa=
l Administrators) and is an overly permissive solution. The Contributor rol=
e provides the necessary permissions at the subscription level without gran=
ting tenant-wide administrative access.</p>
<p><b>B. Owner role</b> - The Owner role in Azure RBAC grants full access t=
o manage all resources, including the ability to delegate access to others.=
 While the Owner role would satisfy the requirement to fully manage the sol=
ution, it also grants the ability to add additional users and assign roles,=
 which is explicitly prohibited by requirement 3. Therefore, the Owner role=
 is not the appropriate choice.</p>
<p><b>D. Reader role</b> - The Reader role in Azure RBAC allows users to on=
ly view resources. It does not grant any permissions to create, modify, or =
delete resources. This role does not meet the requirement that users should=
 be able to fully manage the solution. Therefore, the Reader role is not th=
e appropriate choice.</p>
