<p><b>B. Azure Identity Protection</b> - Azure Identity Protection is prima=
rily focused on detecting and remediating identity-based risks and vulnerab=
ilities, such as leaked credentials, anomalous sign-in activity, and risky =
users. While it contributes to overall security, it doesn't directly addres=
s the requirement of reviewing existing RBAC role assignments to minimize s=
tale permissions. Identity Protection focuses on proactive risk detection, =
not periodic access reviews.</p>
<p><b>C. Azure Active Directory Domain Services (AADDS)</b> - Azure Active =
Directory Domain Services (AADDS) provides managed domain services such as =
domain join, group policy, LDAP, and Kerberos/NTLM authentication. It is us=
ed to support legacy applications that require domain services. AADDS does =
not provide functionality for reviewing RBAC role assignments in Azure subs=
criptions. It's focused on providing domain services for VMs and applicatio=
