aged Instance, Azure Synapse Analytics, and SQL Server databases. While it =
does encrypt data, it primarily focuses on protecting specific columns of s=
ensitive data by encrypting the data within the application before storing =
it in the database. This requires application changes, which contradicts th=
e requirement to minimize management overhead. TDE is a more suitable solut=
ion for encrypting the entire database at rest.</p>
<p><b>C. Azure storage encryption</b> - Azure Storage encryption protects d=
ata at rest by automatically encrypting it before persisting it to Azure St=
orage, and decrypting it before retrieval. This is relevant for Azure Blob =
storage, Azure Files, and Azure Queue storage, but not directly applicable =
to encrypting a SQL Server database. The question specifically asks about e=
ncrypting the database, not general storage accounts.</p>
<p><b>D. SSL certificates</b> - SSL (Secure Sockets Layer) certificates are=
 used to encrypt data in transit, not data at rest. While encrypting data i=
n transit is a requirement, the question specifically asks for a solution t=
o encrypt data at rest. SSL certificates secure the communication channel b=
etween the client and the server, ensuring that data is encrypted while bei=
ng transmitted over the network, but do not encrypt the data stored on the =
database server itself.</p>
